# The judging roster's LOWER BOUND. Machine-readable, read by scripts/sync_personas.py.
#
# This file is a RATCHET. Every name below must be on JUDGING_PERSONA_NAMES. Names may be ADDED;
# removing one is a deliberate reduction of the no-edit guarantee.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING THE RATCHET. Two different things are checked in two different places,
# and only one of them runs on its own:
#
#   the ROSTER falling below this floor  -> sync_personas.py, which `--check` runs at every session
#                                           start. Automatic.
#   a name deleted from THIS FILE        -> `test_the_recorded_floor_has_a_pawl` in the INSTALLED
#                                           suite, and NOTHING RUNS THAT AUTOMATICALLY.
#                                           With the floor lowered,
#                                           check_roster_against_the_record() returns no finding,
#                                           because the floor is what the renderer trusts.
#
# So a deletion from this file is caught only by a manually-run test. That is the weakest link in
# the arrangement and it is stated here rather than left for someone to discover.
#
# That test is ~/.claude/skills/agent-personas/tests/test_repo_sync.py — named by ABSOLUTE path
# because the suite is deliberately not vendored, so in a published copy of this file a relative
# path would name a file that is not there and read as a deleted guard.
#
# It lives inside the skill so the skill is SELF-CONTAINED: a fresh `install.sh` ships it, and a
# missing floor stops being the default state of a new machine. The human-readable argument for the
# roster — why these names, what the guarantee is worth, what it does not cover — stays in
# ~/.claude/docs/decisions.md, which is pinned to this file by
# `test_the_roster_is_pinned_to_the_record_a_human_reads`. Defection must still edit the record a
# human reads, because that property comes from the PIN, not from which file the renderer opens.
#
# One name per line. Blank lines and `#` comments ignored.
